{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511034-takeover","id":1511034,"title":"Takeover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-07T17:41:28-07:00","id":1511034,"title":"Takeover","content":"I've heard some mentions that a very old vampire could possess the body of a younger vampire if diablerized. Assuming this is possible, what would that vampire look like after that, what would his generation look like, what would his clan be, what would his disciplines, blood ties, attributes look like. What would change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T02:21:29-07:00","id":1511058,"title":"","content":"Nothing important","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":".  Bugged forum 05-13-2023, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T02:27:16-07:00","id":1511059,"title":"","content":"It seems uppon editing, my posts end up flagged... when it is approved, wil ldelete the first one<br /> SO!<br /> <br /> The prime example of this is Mithras and Montgomery Coven<br /> Mithras was driven into torpor during the German Blitz of London during World War II. He awoke in 1996 only to be immediately attacked by an entire pack of Lupines. He defeated them, but was exhausted and horribly wounded. Shortly thereafter the fledgling Cainite Monty Coven stumbled upon him and diablerized the methuselah<br /> But the vitae was not so much a gift as an invader, and the Monty Coven that heaved itself out of the more than 3000-year-old ash heap was irrevocably changed.<br /> Monty lacked the power to fully consume the soul of a Cainite as puissant as Mithras and the diablerie was incomplete. He coudl feel the personality of Mithras in his mind and battled with it for control over his body. His Amaranth caused him to drop several generations down to the sixth from the eleventh. The power of Mithras' blood had washed away the Vaulderie of the Sabbat and left him torn with the ancient personality of the Methuselah in his head. Left to his own devices, Monty now strives to battle all who ever dared to command him, although he must battle for control over The ancient soul of Mithras could not devoured so easy.<br /> In the V20 timeline, by the start of the twenty-first century, the battle over Monty Coven's body seems to have cooled, with Mithras gaining control. The new Montgomery Coven is in many ways greater than the sum of his parts: the original Monty was angry and driven, though relatively weak and without focus, while Mithras had almost godlike powers but suffered from the deadening ennui of millenia. Today Coven has the knowledge, wisdom, and much of the power of a methuselah, but still feels the excitement and raw emotions of the recently Embraced. Though he is quiet and subtle in his actions, the now young methuselah is more active than almost any of his ancient peers. His goal is to reclaim Britain as his own realm, independent of any sect or power. Monty's diablerie of Mithras remains an open secret, known by many but hidden from most.<br /> In V5 it is up to the players in Fall of London scenario what happens<br /> BJD had another example, Marry the Black and Michael and the potential story hook of Mythras/Monty's plan to reinvigorate other Ancients (his &quot;friends&quot;) to knock them out of the ennui of ages, by transplanting the soul with diablerie in to a younger host\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T02:47:15-07:00","id":1511060,"title":"","content":"In V20, at least, Diablerie seemed to lead to more of a merging/mixture of two identities than simply a takeover. Such as Monty Coven/Mithras and Mary/Michael, as mentioned. <br /> The Tal'Mahe'Ra supplement added rules. You automatically lose one generation upon successful diablerie, and then you can opt to lose more with continuing contested rolls until you reach the victim's generation or you fail (at which point you suck in the soul being diablerised instead of just the generation). The more dominating of the component personalities is usually the one that defines the personality of whoever walks away. <br /> <br /> At worst the victim's personality (nature and demeanor) are dominant and the vampire walks off with the memories and skills of diablerist and victim. Clan is unchanged. This is also only available to the lowest generations.<br /> <br /> Lesser degrees may include derangements (split personalities, flashbacks, etc), or shifts in ones nature and stuff like that.<br /> <br /> There's some exchange of disciplines/abilities and stuff but I'd have to look it up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T02:58:38-07:00","id":1511061,"title":"","content":"(Posting an addendum instead of editing, because I don't trust the algorithm not to flag me)<br /> <br /> To clarify, when I say &quot;Clan is unchanged&quot; I mean that the vampire that walks off is of the diablerist's clan, not the victim's.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThey also keep the diablerist's backgrounds and I think the victim's too, if it makes sense? Blood bonds are presumably intact. Unless you decide to throw in some Vicissitude, the body is the diablerist's and it doesn't change.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T10:00:30-07:00","id":1511549,"title":"","content":"Another good example is when Tremere diablerized Saulot and spent many centuries battling for control over there shared form and which Saulot would win and for all intents and purposes was Tremere and had knowledge of blood sorcery and that clan's innate weakness. The same with Mithras being consumed by the Assamite Coven and when he won the battle and is now a member of the Banu Haqim clan instead of the Ventrue clan that he was embraced into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}